    "product_id": "51f5531d-1042-42ef-b73f-3ff2ed7ce5b9",
    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 250716\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n1216 AM PDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Quiet and seasonable conditions through at least Wednesday, with\n  signs of a more active pattern returning late in the week.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Today through Saturday.\n\nThe upper level low responsible for precipitation and cooler \ntemperatures the last few days will track east and a zonal flow \npattern will persist aloft for most of the week. This pattern will \npromote dry and stable conditions and seasonable temperatures. \nAfternoon high temperatures will be within a few degrees of normal \nfor this time of year, which for Las Vegas means highs in the upper \n70s. A pattern shift arrives towards the end of the week as a trough \napproaches the west coast and southwesterly flow develops over the \nsouthwestern United States. Potential changes include cooler \ntemperatures, increased winds, and low to moderate (10 to 50 \npercent) chances of precipitation over Halloween weekend. Details \nregarding the timing and location of these impacts will become more \napparent throughout the week. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 06Z Forecast Package... \nNortherly winds are expected to stick around through at least 08Z \nbefore diminishing and becoming light and variable through early \nSunday morning. Winds are expected to become northeast to east in \nthe afternoon with speeds around 7 knots or less. Clouds will \ndissipate overnight with mainly clear skies expected Sunday, \nalthough a few high clouds are expected to spread over the area late \nafternoon. \n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 06Z Forecast Package...Generally clear skies \nwith diminishing winds to less than 10 knots overnight. Skies will \nremain clear through much of Sunday, although high clouds will \ngradually spread across the region in the afternoon. Winds will \ngenerally remain under 10 knots through much of Sunday, with the \nexception of KBIH where afternoon southerly gusts to 15 knots are \npossible.\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Meltzer\nAVIATION...Gorelow\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
